  "question": {
    "text": "<p>At what distance above and below the surface of the earth a body will have same weight? (Take radius of earth as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math>)</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>R</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt><mi>R</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The acceleration due to gravity at a height <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi></math> above the surface of the Earth is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>The acceleration due to gravity at a depth <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi></math> below the surface of the Earth is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mi>h</mi><mi>R</mi></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>According to the given problem,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Equations (1), (2) and (3) imply that</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>g</mi><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>h</mi><mi>R</mi></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mi>h</mi><mi>R</mi></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>h</mi><mi>R</mi></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>4</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Take <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>h</mi><mi>R</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></math></p><p>So, from equation (4), it follows that</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p>"
  }
}